g without representing?”</title><link href="https://ttoe-dj.github.io/posts/2025/Clark1994/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Notes on Clark &amp;amp; Toribio (1994) “Doing without representing?”"/><published>2025-08-27T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-08-27T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://ttoe-dj.github.io/posts/2025/Clark1994</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://ttoe-dj.github.io/posts/2025/Clark1994/"><![CDATA[<iframe src="https://rainbow-scorpion-b48.notion.site/ebd/27233a0c36ae80c39a44d4b57f7b904d" width="100%" height="600" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen=""/>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="notes"/><category term="experience"/><category term="agent"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Faqism</title><link href="https://ttoe-dj.github.io/posts/2025/Faqism/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Faqism"/><published>2025-08-11T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-08-11T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://ttoe-dj.github.io/posts/2025/Faqism</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://ttoe-dj.github.io/posts/2025/Faqism/"><![CDATA[<p>I’m a faqist. I practice faqism.</p> <p>Faqism (pronounced /ˈfäkiz(ə)m/) means what it says, faq ism.</p> <p>An X-ist says: I hope/like/believe that the world conforms to X-ism. Therefore I support ideas in favor of X-ism.</p> <p>A faqist says: I want to learn truths about the world, whatever they might be. Faq A-ism. Faq B-ism. Faq C-ism. Faq all isms. Faq prejudices.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="polemics"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[I’m a faqist. I practice faqism.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">What’s the status of singularity in the correct theory of quantum gravity (if there is any)</title><link href="https://ttoe-dj.github.io/posts/2025/SingularityMarket/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="What’s the status of singularity in the correct theory of quantum gravity (if there is any)"